---
/*
  SheetHeader — the title row every admin sheet opens with: a heading, a ✕, and
  the rule under them.

  ⚠ THIS IS [29 · §6](docs/plans/archive/29-one-owner-per-fact.md), BUILT — the
  piece that plan named "the sheet skeleton" and left for last because it has the
  largest blast radius. Its shape was decided 2026-08-09 and this keeps it: the
  header, the close button and the `aria-labelledby` wiring, dropped INSIDE each
  existing `<form>` so implicit submit survives. It does not touch footers — only
  four of those ever matched, `FragmentSheet` and `LogSheet` have none at all,
  and hoisting one out of a form would break `type="submit"` in seven places.

  ⚠ IT IS TWO COMPONENTS AND 29 SPECIFIED ONE, AND THAT IS A DEVIATION WITH A
  REASON. 29 said "header + error line", assuming they are adjacent. In the tree
  they are adjacent in five sheets and separated in three — `FragmentSheet` and
  `SongSheet` put a tab strip between them, `TagSheet` a paragraph. A single
  shell rendering both would fight three of eight, and 29's own escape hatch
  ("if the slot contract fights any one sheet, leave that sheet out … a forced
  abstraction beats nothing at being worse") would leave the shell serving five.
  Two small components serve all eight and constrain nothing about what sits
  between them. See `SheetError.astro` for the other half.

  ⚠ THE VERSION THAT WON IS `SongSheet`'s, WHICH WAS THE DIVERGENT ONE. Plan 38 ·
  §3 found it copied its neighbour on 2026-08-11 and then drifted twice — and
  both drifts were improvements: `truncate` on the title and `shrink-0` on the ✕
  make it **the only sheet that survives a long title**. Everywhere else, a long
  heading pushed the ✕ off the edge of the dialog. So the shell takes the
  outlier's shape and every sheet gets the fix, which is the opposite of what
  a consistency sweep usually does and is the whole reason to look at drift
  before flattening it.

  ⚠ LOGSHEET IS DELIBERATELY NOT A CONSUMER, as 29 decided. Its header is
  `px-5 py-3.5` with a `text-lg` title inside a `modal-dialog` rather than a
  drawer — a smaller box for one line of prose, not a drawer for a record — and
  forcing it to `px-6 py-4`/`text-xl` would grow the one sheet whose point is
  that it is quick. Seven owners beats eight.
*/
interface Props {
  /**
   * The `<h2>`'s id. The caller wires its own `<dialog aria-labelledby>` to it —
   * the dialog element is the caller's, so the id has to be too.
   */
  titleId: string;
  /** The heading, when it is a plain string. Otherwise use the default slot. */
  title?: string;
}
const { titleId, title } = Astro.props;
---

<header class="border-base-300 flex shrink-0 items-center justify-between border-b px-6 py-4">
  <h2 id={titleId} class="font-display truncate text-xl">{title}<slot /></h2>
  {
    /* `data-close` is the contract `wireSheetDismiss` binds by default, so every
      sheet's ✕ routes through the same exit as Escape and the backdrop (ADR
      0032). SongSheet used to spell it `data-sng-close` and pass the selector in
      by hand — a second name for the one thing the ADR made uniform. */
  }
  <button type="button" data-close class="text-base-content/50 hover:text-base-content shrink-0" aria-label="Close"
    >✕</button
  >
</header>
